<title>UK: Toyota says Euro sales rose 7 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Toyota says Euro sales rose 7 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Europe said on Wednesday that its European sales rose seven percent in 1996 compared to 1995, with 412,000 units sold.</p>
<p>Market share for the group rose slightly to 2.6 percent and the group is now targeting sales of 450,000 units in 1997, growing to 600,000 units in 1998. Alan Marsh, vice-chairman of Toyota Motor Europe, said the group would launch an aggressive campaign to strengthen its European presence, describing the region as &quot;perhaps the most competitive in the world.&quot;</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
